   My $.02 on the other subthreads, just to confuse matters: I think
speed pills should prevent sleep, for consistency with the source mythos
(presumably caffeine, amphetamines, or some other stimulant). They
certainly shouldn't cause hallucination. The headache pill--succubus
interaction seems so obvious that it really can't be left out, unless
the name of the pill is changed. To me, "repeated word" equals "pun or
other interaction."

My other comments:
   "Sleeping pills temporarily cure insomnia." Huh? As in, they make you
fall asleep, right? (Taking speed and sleeping pills together should
probably have some bad effects.)

   "Headache pill" is not an expression with which I'm familiar; is it
a Britishism? In real life, I'd use the term "Tylenol" (which Nethack
can't use because of copyright) or "painkiller". My first suggestion,
though, is "analgesic", as a nod to Infocom's HHGTTG adventure game
and because it looks like a Nethacky vocabulary word to me. ("Analgesic"
and "painkiller" are both more general terms than "headache pill",
though, so they might force some kind of interaction with other kinds
of pain: leg pain from kicking a wall, for example.)
   Ditto "antibiotics pill", which at least ought to be "antibiotic pill".
"Pill of penicillin", perhaps? I don't have any good suggestion here.

   It should be possible to kill yourself by overdosing on speed, headache,
sleeping, or (hallucination?), if you try hard enough. And maybe wishing,
just because "killed by an overdose of wishing pills" would make a great
tombstone.
   Overdosing on some pills might induce vomiting, too, I think, but you'd
have to consult the source mythos.

my $.02,
